course: dictionary
lesson: 11902
title: Bugle: a brass signal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bugle is a brass instrument, like a small, simple trumpet. It has no valves, so it can play only a few notes. «The bugle sounded at dawn, and the soldiers woke up.» The bugle is the instrument, and sounded tells you it made a loud call.
explain: Read the words around bugle to work out what it does. «The bugle played a short tune before the parade.» A parade is a march, and a short tune is a signal, so a bugle is used to call people to something.
explain: Music teachers say the bugle makes its notes by changing the shape of your lips. «Mia blew into the brass bugle and made one clear note.» Blew and note are clues: a bugle is played by blowing, not by pressing keys.
fact: A bugle is a brass instrument, like a small, simple trumpet.
fact: A bugle has no valves, so it plays only a few notes.
fact: In the past, armies used bugles to give signals such as wake up, march or attack.
fact: On remembrance days, the «Last Post» is played on a bugle.
fact: Scouts and marching bands may play bugles.
exercise: «The bugle sounded at dawn, and the soldiers woke up.» What is a bugle? | A large wooden drum | A kind of flower | *A small brass instrument with no valves | A tall tower on a castle
exercise: «The bugle played a short tune before the parade.» What was the bugle used for here? | To cook the breakfast | To catch fish from a river | To sweep the path clean | *To play a short tune as a signal
exercise: In history, what did armies use bugles for? | To sell food at the market | *To give signals, such as wake up, march or attack | To teach people to swim | To make soup
exercise: «Mia blew into the brass bugle and made one clear note.» What clue tells you a bugle is played by blowing? | Mia smiled at her friend | The parade was long | The brass shone in the sun | *Blew into the bugle
test: «The soldiers heard the bugle and marched out at once.» What did the bugle signal? | *March | Go swimming | Sleep | Dinner is ready
test: What is a bugle NOT? | A brass instrument | *An instrument with many valves and keys | Played by blowing | Used to play short tunes
exam: «The Scouts gathered at dawn, and a bugle called them to the flag.» What is the bugle doing here? | Cooking porridge for the Scouts | Hiding from the rain | Washing the flag | *Calling people together with a signal
